{
 "allowed_sentences": [
  "In ACTINV's P188 sidecar, 62 TENDL-2025 reactions on 42 target nuclides take IRDFF-II's covariance, expressed about TENDL-2025's cross section and including the difference between the two evaluations, with IRDFF-II's short-range variances as IRDFF-II gives them; every other covariance is TENDL-2025's, unchanged.",
  "For FNS iron after 5 minutes' irradiation, the cross-section part of the relative standard deviation of the Mn56 activity is 36.4% with TENDL-2025's covariances and 1.1% with P188's, at 66 s after shutdown.",
  "For FNS iron after 5 minutes' irradiation, the cross-section part of the relative standard deviation of the Mn54 activity is 42% with TENDL-2025's covariances and 2% with P188's, at 66 s after shutdown.",
  "For FNS iron after 5 minutes' irradiation, the cross-section part of the relative standard deviation of the Fe53 activity is 40.1% with TENDL-2025's covariances and 8.76% with P188's, at 66 s after shutdown.",
  "For FNS iron after 5 minutes' irradiation, the cross-section part of the relative standard deviation of the Cr51 activity is 67.9% with TENDL-2025's covariances and 1.82% with P188's, at 66 s after shutdown.",
  "For FNS iron after 5 minutes' irradiation, the cross-section part of the relative standard deviation of the Mn57 activity is 38.7% with TENDL-2025's covariances and 38.7% with P188's, at 66 s after shutdown.",
  "With P188's sidecar, on two FNS-spectrum point problems (iron, and a nickel, cobalt, aluminium, tungsten and niobium mixture), ACTINV's first-order activity band agreed with the spread of 200 sampled solves within the registered limit on all 55 tested (nuclide, time) pairs; the ratio of first-order to sampled variance ranged from 0.856 to 1.27."
